description: Jani hackathon project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This workspace is Jani, a Small AI entry for the World Bank x Hack-Nation hackathon (Annex B, Agriculture). Deadline Sun 4 Oct 2026, 15:00 CEST; freeze 13:30.

- Read `kb/MASTER_PROMPT.md` before any task. It is the source of truth.
- If the user names an agent (research, ml, engine, ui, content-voice, docs, pitch, qa, judge, redteam, mathematician, agronomist, ux-designer, user-simulator, security-privacy, release-manager), follow `kb/agents/<name>.md` and edit only the paths it owns (see `kb/OWNERSHIP.md`).
- Shared types and formats: `kb/CONTRACTS.md`. Status: `kb/STATUS.md`. Settled decisions: `kb/DECISIONS.md` (do not reopen).
- The git repo is `app/`. Lovable also pushes to `main`: pull before push, small commits prefixed with the agent name, never force-push.
- Never commit or print `app/backend/.env`. Never put secrets in `VITE_*` variables (they ship to the browser).
- No runtime LLM or AI API calls in the client. All farmer-facing text comes from `src/content/answers.json`.
- Plain British English, no em dashes.
